      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli): bind capability CLI media input reads to descriptor size",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `readCliInputFileSafely` function in `src/cli/capability-cli/media-output.ts` reads input files for media capability commands with a TOCTOU-prone pattern: a path-based `stat` validates the size, then a separate `await fs.readFile(path)` reads the content. Between the stat and the read, a file could be swapped with a much larger one, potentially causing OOM.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMedia input files are user-supplied paths that could be symlink-swapped or grown between validation and consumption. Opening the file first and binding the read to the size observed on that descriptor eliminates the race while preserving the existing unlimited-input contract.\n\n## What Changed\n\nReplaced the path-based `stat` + `readFile` pattern with a descriptor-bound exact read:\n\n```typescript\nconst handle = await fs.open(resolvedPath, \"r\");\ntry {\n  const stat = await handle.stat();\n  if (!stat.isFile()) throw new Error(\"not a regular file\");\n  const size = stat.size;\n  const buffer = Buffer.alloc(size);\n  let offset = 0;\n  while (offset < size) {\n    const { bytesRead } = await handle.read(buffer, offset, size - offset, offset);\n    if (bytesRead === 0) return buffer.subarray(0, offset);\n    offset += bytesRead;\n  }\n  return buffer;\n} finally {\n  await handle.close();\n}\n```\n\nKey points:\n- `fs.promises.open()` returns a `FileHandle`; `stat()` and the read both operate on the same descriptor.\n- The read is bounded to the validated `stat.size`, so a concurrent writer cannot grow the file after validation.\n- The existing unlimited-input contract is preserved; no new per-file or aggregate caps are introduced.\n- `try/finally` guarantees `handle.close()` even when exceptions are thrown.\n\n## User Impact\n\n| Before | After |\n|--------|-------|\n| Path-based `stat` followed by `fs.readFile` is vulnerable to swap/grow races. | Descriptor-bound read uses the size observed at open time, closing the TOCTOU window. |\n| Concurrent multi-file scheduling was implicit. | Explicit `Promise.all` around the new helper keeps concurrent reads while making them safer. |\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Integration tests\n\nAll 109 capability CLI integration tests pass on the exact PR head `0d9b01639c64fd5fa101a612859ac89b731a4f95`:\n\n```\n✓ |cli| src/cli/capability-cli.test.ts (109 tests) 3157ms\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  109 passed (109)\n```\n\n### Real CLI invocation\n\nA real `openclaw capability image edit` invocation was run against the PR head. The input file was read through the descriptor-bound path and successfully forwarded to the image generation provider.\n\nCommand (run in a clean worktree at head `0d9b01639c64`):\n\n```bash\nexport OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR=/tmp/openclaw-proof-state\nexport OPENCLAW_QA_ALLOW_LOCAL_IMAGE_PROVIDER=1\nopenclaw capability image edit \\\n  --file /tmp/openclaw-proof-input.png \\\n  --prompt \"make background transparent\" \\\n  --model openai/gpt-image-1.5 \\\n  --output-format png \\\n  --json\n```\n\nResult:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"ok\": true,\n  \"capability\": \"image.edit\",\n  \"transport\": \"local\",\n  \"provider\": \"openai\",\n  \"model\": \"gpt-image-1.5\",\n  \"attempts\": [],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"/tmp/openclaw-proof-state/media/generated/image-1---70de0f12-216b-4eaf-9569-2cea0a98154a.png\",\n      \"mimeType\": \"image/png\",\n      \"size\": 70,\n      \"width\": 1,\n      \"height\": 1,\n      \"revisedPrompt\": \"mocked edit result\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"ignoredOverrides\": []\n}\n```\n\nThe provider endpoint in this run was a local mock returning a 1x1 PNG; the redacted invocation proves the CLI correctly reads the user-supplied media input file through the new descriptor-bound helper and completes the end-to-end `image.edit` pipeline.\n",
